# R7: raw third-party market data is never committed.
# Anchored to the repo root (`/data/`, not `data/`): an unanchored pattern
# matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth, which silently shadowed
# `src/data/` (a real package, not the cache dir) and swallowed
# `src/data/__init__.py` from every commit since Phase 0 without error -
# `git add` skips ignored paths silently unless forced. Fixed here; the
# missing `__init__.py` is restored to tracking in the same commit.
#
# `/data/*` (not `/data/`) ignores the directory's CONTENTS, not the
# directory itself, so the per-subdirectory negations below actually take
# effect: git cannot re-include a file inside a directory the parent
# pattern already excludes, so `/data/` + `!/data/raw/.gitkeep` was dead
# (docs/DECISIONS.md) and every .gitkeep below was silently untracked.
# Each subdirectory needs its own re-include-dir / exclude-contents /
# re-include-.gitkeep triplet.
/data/*
!/data/raw/
!/data/interim/
!/data/processed/
/data/raw/*
!/data/raw/.gitkeep
/data/interim/*
!/data/interim/.gitkeep
/data/processed/*
!/data/processed/.gitkeep

# R8: secrets
.env

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
mlruns/
*.parquet
